As Kent Paul Dolan requested, this is my priest ascension.

BTW, how's the formatting? I tried hard
to make this more legible, but I have no
idea what you're seeing.

Patrick
St: 12 Dx; 15 Co: 14 In:7 Wi: 18 Ch: 9
Human
Game Patron: Raijin (neutral)

Now, I can't say I care much for the priest,
because as far as I can
see he is a middle-range class, like the monk. He possesses
neither the immense strength and melee capability
of the Melee Monsters (
barbarian, Valkyrie, Samurai), nor the ranged
weapons of the shooting classes (ranger, rogue) nor
the swiss-army-knife capability of the tourist
nor the power of the wizard. He is too strong to be
played as a pacifist,
and too weak to be played as Melee Monster.  Further,
he is restricted in dagger (my favorite weapon) and can
only reach basic in bow or crossbow.

So he's not much of a range fighter.

He does, however, have one bright, redeeming
characteristic. This is, that he can see at a glance
whether something is cursed or not. This
makes sifting through armor much easier, since I no
longer have to pet-check
(a process I do not find foolproof) to avoid
cursed -N armor.  Thus, I can
find decent armor much more rapidly than
I would otherwise.

Begin the game by a simple map-n-dive -- map
out the entire level,
then go down.   I am taking most of the kills, so my
dog Bark doesn't level up until turn 2345. I find a
blindfold, and soon enough encounter
a floating eye. I blindfold myself and kill
it to gain telepathy, which will
stand me in good stead for the rest of the game.

At this point, I only have a few crude daggers
in which I am, of course,
unskilled. I'm concerned with my lack of ranged
weapons, so I decide to raid the
first floor of the Gnomish mines in hopes of
getting armor and ranged weapons
from the gnomes, dwarves, and arrow traps there. This
pays off handsomely, as
I find elvish mithril, dwarvish helm and iron shoes
to give me an AC of -3.

Continue on down into the maze to find a bones level.
I *remember* this one ... a nymph on the level stole
everything and left me totally
naked, without *anything*. The character tried beating
the nymph bare-handed, but it
didn't work. His death was not long delayed.

I am determined not to let it happen again!
I rummage through my inventory and
come up with a wand of magic missile. I have
telepathy, so I stalk the nymph
and start blasting away.   I drain nearly all the
charges from the wand but in the
end I kill the *****.  I consider the price well worth paying.
Clear the bones
pile she left from the old character and acquire
+3 hooded cloak and +1 boots.

Continue exploring the main branch, falling
through a trap door
and getting separated from my pet at turn 9116.  Still,
keep exploring and successfully acquire sleep resistance
from an elf, and poison resistance from a quivering blob.
This makes me
breathe a little easier, as the most likely early game instakills
are behind me.

I get my first real scare at turn 10985, when I am cornered and
trapped by a leocrotta and an owlbear.  I can't engrave "E" because
I have nothing but my fingers and my dexterity is too low to
properly engrave it.  And these two creatures are hammering me!
As a last resort, I pray and get my hit points back.  I succeed
in meleeing the monsters to death and continue on down. Phew!

Things take a turn for the better on turn 11442 when I find a ring
of conflict!  Cold resistance follows quickly.  Then I find a rust
trap and corrode my +2 mace.

Then I make a mistake. Entering sokoban at turn 15557, I
accidentally
trap my dog on the wrong side of a boulder.  I can't
get him out.

I could kill him, of course... at the cost of angering
my deity and
I am too dependent on prayer at the moment.  So I decide to
go back
and wander the main maze, looking for something like a
wand of teleport which I could use to free him.

I eventually find a wand of teleport. I also get
fire resistance from a red naga and speed from a
wand of speed monster.

Back to sokoban. I lose 3 luck points in short order.
Once for teleporting an object and freeing my pet,
once for goofing up and trapping myself with a boulder,
forcing myself to pick-axe out .And, because I was
dumb enough to do this on the top level of Soko,
am forced to read a scroll of earth to finish the level.
That's three points of luck in short order.   Nonetheless,
I clear Sokoban and pick up my prize -- a bag of holding --
on turn 19958.

Turn 22718 is significant, as I find an uncursed polearm.
I consider this critical for a priest, since it is the only
ranged weapon that a priest can reach 'skilled' at. Plus I
am in love with it's versatility, allowing me to hit anything
in a two square radius of my character regardless of whether
I'm in a direct line or not. I can even reach over monsters
to hit a monster behind the first one, allowing me to use
weak monsters as meat shields against strong ones.

Off to the Gnome mines to get the luckstone.  I always have
trouble with the mines below minetown, and I am not
disappointed this time.

I step on a polytrap and become a new man. Stats:
St: 18 Dx: 15 Co: 18 In: 9 Wi: 18 Ch: 10

Not bad, really.

I encounter an air elemental (presumably from the
same poly trap)
which takes me down to 29/80 hp.
I also encounter a Mumak, but I use my greater speed to
stay away from him. I shoot him full of poisoned arrows and my
dog Bark finishes him off. Acquire the luckstone at turn
28235,
and I waste no time maxing out my luck
with the closest friendly unicorn.

I have by now exhausted the wand of teleport I
had earlier used
to free my pet in Sokoban ... or so I think.
In keeping with
policy, I break it in order to clear the dungeon
of useless scrap.

It turns out there is still at least one charge left.
There is a
magical explosion and ... WHEEE! Awaaay we go!

Continuing down into the maze, fnding a co-aligned
altar and a priest on level 17, from whom I buy
3 points of protection, reaching an AC of -17.
As you can see, the ability
to see b/u/c status has enabled me to find some
excellent armor in a hurry, and
I am now much tougher than I was.  I perform a water prayer
at this altar
and receive the gift of stealth on turn 31223.

On turn 31272 I arrive in a bigroom on level 12.

I slip on a ring of conflict and allow the monsters to
kill each other.
I am approached by a g. cube. I engrave "E" on the ground
and shoot it from a distance with a bow and arrows.

I must say at this point that a bow and arrows
was my permanent ranged weapon in this game, along with
my polearm, because the priest can reach 'basic'
in it, which is as good as just about any other
skill he has. There's also lots and lots of
arrows in the arrow traps,
and the individual arrows are quite light.

There are some cockatrices on the level. They clear the level.
I then
kill them with my bow and arrows. Next, I begin
smashing statues with
a pickaxe to see what treasures I may find ... and
one of those treasures is a pair of
boots of speed!

Continue down into the maze, and am moderately
amused when a nymph
opens a door that turns out to be trapped.

KA-BOOM!

She is blown to smithereens!  Hee.

You would think at this point, that I was
nigh-invulnerable with my
low AC, my boots of speed, my ranged weapons,
and my ring of conflict.

I was swiftly brought down to earth on turn 34070
when I was
ambushed by an energy vortex. I am not shock-resistant
and am rapidly
brought down to 6/95 hit points.  Desperate, I pray and
receive no
answer beyond 'well pleased'.

Thanks a lot, RNG.

One chance left; I have a wand of teleport. I zap
my self with it and excape
elsewhere on the level.

79 turns pass as I try to heal up.  The energy vortex
chases me down and
I am at 41/95 hp. I know I can't survive another ride,
so as a last resort
I zap a wand of polymorph at it.  It turns into a vampire bat.

A vampire bat? Against a -17 AC? No problem.  Smack him down
and continue my way down.

On turn 34447, I arrive at a graveyard level on level 16.
I spend
considerable time luring wraiths up the stairs and achieve
level 14,
becoming eligible for the quest. This is followed by level 15,
at which
point I receive the warning intrinsic.

Traveling on and feeling cocky, I step on a polymorph trap
at turn 34975
and turn into a baby grey dragon, smashing my +3 cloak
and my elvish mithril.

I being looking around to find replacement stuff.
My notes are fragmentary,
but I believed I had stored mithril and cloaks in a
cache above the dungeon.

I traveled back up and replaced my armor. I then suicided
my dragon form
by throwing my mace up into the air until it
killed my dragon form and
I became human again.

On turn 36075, my dog Bark is killed by an invisible stalker.
Fortunately, I can cast create familiar. I cast it and receive
a pet little dog.

Turn 39766.  Things get interesting. I step
into a throne room ... and in this throne
room is a black dragon!

Fortunately, it is in a corner against a wall,
trapped behind row upon row of sleeping monsters.
I have stealth, so they won't wake up.

I remember that a black dragon needs to be in a
direct line to use its breath weapon, but I don't
need a direct line to use a polearm, which I am
skilled in. So I move such that I am in an L-shaped pattern
from him and stab repeatedly with my polearm. Unable
to reach
me and unable to bring his breath weapon to bear, he
soon succumbs
and gives me disintegration resistance.

Some turns later,  I am assaulted by an angel and melee it.
It starts to get the better of me.   I am in trouble, so
I pray. I get crowned, and Vorpal blade drops at my feet.
Nice, but
that's not hit points and I'm down to 37/128.
I zap myself with a
wand of teleport, drink a potion of full healing,
then hunt down and
kill the creature. All well and good, but I see an
ettin pick up the
Vorpal blade.


...

I'm in trouble.

...

The Ettin has one weakness, however. It is slow.
I pull out my polearm
and engage him from a distance, using my greater speed
to stay away from
that nasty weapon. I succeed in killing it, then
take the vorpal blade.

Back to the throne room, which is still a work in progress.
I find
a wand of invisibility and waste no time zapping
myself with it.
Eventually clearing the room, sit on the throne
and receive a genocide,
which I use on master mind flayers. A little
more looking reveal
a pair of boots of jumping, which I keep.
I am now on level 24.

Continue my exploration, but step on a
level teleport trap which takes me
from level 27 to level 5.  Deciding to
redeem the time, I visit
Itzhak and buy the 7 candles I
need to finish the game.  I also find
a book of stone to flesh which I memorize.

On turn 43772, I encounter my first lich. I stand
on "E" and beat him
to death. Sometime later, I encounter a
gelatinous cube.  Since
there is no one else around, I try on unidentified rings
while fighting
it and am gratified to find a ring of free action,
another important item.

Find a cockatrice next on level 18 which I had
previously cleared.
There are a number of statues here.  I cast
stone to flesh on them
to bring them to life.  2 are hostile and die quickly,
but the next
two are peaceful and I let them go.
 A yellow dragon donates scales,
and I use a scroll of enchant armor to make dragon
scale mail from it. This
will hold me in good stead until I can
find grey or silver dargon armor.

Turn 44895. Arrive medusa level and immediately
receive a mind flayer
alert.  He is in Medusa's palace.  I catch a quasit
between myself and the mind
flayer. I shrug off the quasit's pitiful attacks
and stab away with my polearm,
eventually killing the mind flayer. Medusa lasts
only a few more turns, just long
enough for me to share her a mirror, then
pick-axe the body apart.

I cast stone to flesh on the statues in Medusa's lair
(this is why I pick-axed her
body -- I didn't want her coming back!) and bring many
humans to life, including
Perseus. Perseus fights but I kill him and take his
amulet of reflection. Of the
remaining humans only one of them -- a priest by
the name of Augustine -- is friendly.
I let him go.

At some point along here, I tamed another dog. True to form,
on turn 45439 he heats
a doppleganger corpse and becomes a kobold shaman, who follows me
around for a long time.

On turn 45649 I crack the passtune to the castle. I typically
use the drawbridge as a weapon in this situation, but
it's hard on monster
inventory so I slip on my ring of conflict instead.
The only major problem is a
golden naga, which I hunt and kill using my bow and arrows,
engraving "E" with a
wand of digging once to make him run away.

Continue into the castle and sit on the castle throne, which
saps 5 points of
constitution. Too bad I have a unicorn
horn which gives them right back.

By turn 46421 the castle is cleared.
However, while wandering the castle
I encounter a titan
which I promptly shoot with poisoned arrows,
which I have
been saving for just such an occasion. It
counters with
a monster swarm. I counter with a ring of conflict.
Somehow I
get paralyzed and hit a couple times but
I recover
at 89/133. Finally, I close and kill
the Titan with  Vorpal Blade.

Time for wishing. I wish for
a blessed spellbook of identify (solves
many problems),
blessed +2 gray dragon scale mail,
and 2 scrolls of genocide. Use them
to wipe out mind flayers and all Lich-class creatures.
I also rustproof my polearm.

Head back up to the mines and donate
most of the cash I found, reaching a naked
AC of 2.  I next head for the
quest level and reach it on turn 48081.

There are a number of wraiths here, and I manage to
eat a few to reach epic level 20.

At turn 51087, I face off with Nalzok the quest nemesis.
I engrave an "E" with fire on the downstairs, then
step off the stairs, zap him with a wand of magic missile,
then back onto the stairs and the "E" there. Sure as sunrise,
here he comes. I beat him to death with Vorpal blade.

At this point I find that my former dog now kobold shaman
is pretty useless.
I can do my own b/u/c ID and he isn't fighting anyone.
 It'd be murder to take him
into Gehennom. I leave him in the care of the priests
on Home 1.  Who knows? As a shaman, he may be the
first kobold in our order.

Hit Fort Ludios on turn 52876.  One of the soldiers
was packing a wand of death but was unable to use it.
I acquire it at full charge. Kick open Croesus' door
on turn 53546 wearing my ring of conflict.

While Croesus is busy fighting his bodyguards, I shoot
him dead
with poisoned arrows. His throne yields a genoicide
which I use on
krakens.  Not too much later a mordor orc drops a
blessed scroll of
genocide (good thing he didn't read it!)
I use it to wipe out all ;.

So much for eels, electric eels, and their instakill .

Begin preparing for final descent.  Buy a last
point of protection to
reach a naked AC of -1 and a regular AC of -20.
Quaff some gain
abilities and a blessed potion of enlightenment
to reach an int of 11.

I nonetheless bless any books I wish to read.

Continuing my preparations, I alchemize healing
and gain energy potions
and bring my hp up to 208.  My current stats are:


St: 18/24 Dx: 18 Co: 18 In: 17 (+1 for helm of brilliance),
wis 19 (+1 for helm of brilliance),
ch: 17

I proceed to quaff 3 blessed potions of enlightenment,
bringing my int
score to 19.

I quaff smoky potions ( I believe they are
